hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1785","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Qais (Abu Musa Ash'ari) رضي الله عنه that the Messenger of Allah صلى الله عليه وسلم said: ""There are two gardens of silver, their utensils and all their articles are of silver, and there are also two gardens of gold, their utensils and articles are of gold, and in Paradise of Eden, between the people and their Lord, there will be only the veil of Majesty and Greatness, which will be over the blessed Face of the Lord."
"1786","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Qais (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""In Paradise, there is a tent made of a hollow pearl, and the width of this tent is sixty miles. In every corner of it will be the wives of the Muslims; those in one corner will not be able to see those in the other corners, and the believing men will go around to them...."" (The rest of the hadith has been mentioned in the commentary of Surah Ar-Rahman.)"
